The file contains the data files containing the variables, the Python code and the result tables of model 3.
Model 3 is a monthly regression set up to test H3.
H3 assumes that when external pollution contribution from PRD is high, HK faces greater external pressure (increase of marginal damage from external pollutants) and will respond by tightening local controls (increase abatement). 
Model 3 estimate short- and long-term associations between PRD effect and HK abatement. 
To be more specific, it intends to measure how HK abatement (which is the dependent variable (DV) of model 3) depends on the extend of PRD effect. 
"Emission intensity" (HK emissions / real GDP)  is being used as a proxy of abatement response.
